# Public IP vs Private IP

| Feature                    | Public IP              | Private IP           |
| -------------------------- | ---------------------- | -------------------- |
| Used on                    | Internet               | Local network        |
| Globally unique            | Yes                    | No                   |
| Example                    | `8.8.8.8`              | `192.168.1.10`       |
| Directly Internet-routable | Generally yes          | No                   |
| Common use                 | Internet communication | Home/office networks |

---

# IPv4 vs IPv6

| Feature       | IPv4                        | IPv6                        |
| ------------- | --------------------------- | --------------------------- |
| Full Form     | Internet Protocol version 4 | Internet Protocol version 6 |
| Address Size  | 32-bit                      | 128-bit                     |
| Example       | `192.168.1.10`              | `2001:db8::1`               |
| Separator     | Dot `.`                     | Colon `:`                   |
| Address Space | Smaller                     | Extremely large             |

---

# Quick Revision

```text
IPv4       → 32-bit IP address
IPv6       → 128-bit IP address
Public IP  → Used on the Internet
Private IP → Used inside local networks
Subnetting → Divides a network into smaller networks
```

### Easy Way to Remember

> **IPv4 → 32-bit addressing**

> **IPv6 → 128-bit addressing**

> **Public IP → Internet**

> **Private IP → Local network**

> **Subnetting → Network → Smaller networks**
